      "minimum_trials": 3,
      "maximum_trials": 5,
      "noise_threshold_range_over_median": 0.1,
      "sampling": "Sequential subprocesses. Alternate reference/populate order each trial. If either engine has (max-min)/median > 0.10 after three trials, extend the pair to five. The later DSB text extension reran only noisy populate; its stable native reference retained three trials.",
      "summary": "Median wall time, minimum and maximum; independent medians for bytes and flush, median of per-sample wall-plus-flush totals.",
      "timed_region": "Monotonic clock around subprocess launch through exit; includes GNU time wrapper, startup, generation, encoding, writes and close. Excludes output setup, metadata scans, hashes, final fsync and cleanup. A resource monitor polls every 0.2 seconds.",
      "flush": "File-output samples attempt fsync on each output file after process timing. Historical harness ignored OSError from fsync and did not sync directories: totals are attempted file-flush measurements, not a durability guarantee. Memory/discard flush fields are null; original near-zero empty-loop timings are omitted.",
      "arrow": "Generate and drop RecordBatches with no IPC serialization or file output. Upstream reference uses an external shared 32-thread adapter, default 8000-row batches, and all data tables.",
      "discard": "For controls, create per-output-file symlinks to /dev/null using the preceding SSD file manifest. Also create .inprogress symlinks and pass --overwrite for tpcgen-cli. Verify zero actual file bytes after each attempt. Generator, encoder and write calls still execute; encoded byte throughput is not measured.",
      "threads": "32 threads for populate and tpcgen; SSB native serial and DSB native use one core; SSB native -C 32 uses 32 processes. Native DSB uses its documented serial all-table invocation to respect metadata dependencies.",
      "warmup_runs": 0,
      "global_page_cache_drops": false,
      "seed": "No seed override; implementation defaults, with the explicit command arguments recorded per measurement.",
      "parquet": "Snappy defaults on both tested Rust writers; byte equality is not expected from different batching/file layouts. TPC-DS reference also emits dbgen_version.parquet.",
